# H1: hand the cards back to production. This is the LAST job of the window and it runs even when any earlier job failed, stalled or hung
# (a hang can leave a card wedged with production down): the status of every board, the all-four reset, the fabric re-measure (the
# four-card probe: the ring, the link count and the collectives timed; it must pass before production serves), then the node agent starts
# again and waits for its container to answer /v1/models. The agent serves the rig daemon's local :latest, which this window did NOT move,
# so the placement the owner's /deploy then makes is TODAY'S PRODUCTION RECIPE (profile c2-packed-tp4: audits off, the pinned sampler in the verify trace).
# NEVER place a gate arm or this window's image: not c2-packed-tp4-best-sdpa, not any gate-only profile.
# AN OWNER /deploy IS STILL NEEDED, always, to place today's production recipe or anything new: this job starts the agent with nothing placed; it never includes a deploy, a :latest retag or
# a placement call. If the fabric re-measure fails the job stops before agentstart: production stays down until a board is healed.
# Pass: all four boards enumerate after the reset, the fabric probe passes, /v1/models answers Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B:tt and a chat completes,
# and the engine log shows profile c2-packed-tp4 with the audits off and QWEN_FAST_PACKED_SAMPLER_IN_TRACE=1.
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min, fabric probe 5-10 min, agent start and model load 10-15 min: 25 min.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/sdpa-long window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/sdpa-long and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card,
# a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status reset fabric agentstart
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-3a
